From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: System Electronics <ci@sysele.local>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] waflib: fix compatibility with python-3.12

Python 3.12 removes the deprecated 'imp' module entirely (it had only
been deprecated, with a warning, since 3.4/3.11), so importing waflib
now fails before do_configure even starts:

  ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'imp'

The only real usage in this old waflib snapshot is
imp.new_module(WSCRIPT_FILE) in Context.load_module(), which is
exactly what types.ModuleType(name) does; switch to that instead of
'imp'.

Upstream-Status: Backport
Signed-off-by: System Electronics <ci@sysele.local>
---
 waflib/Context.py | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/waflib/Context.py b/waflib/Context.py
--- a/waflib/Context.py
+++ b/waflib/Context.py
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 #! /usr/bin/env python
 # encoding: utf-8
 # WARNING! Do not edit! https://waf.io/book/index.html#_obtaining_the_waf_file

-import os,re,imp,sys
+import os,re,types,sys
 from waflib import Utils,Errors,Logs
 import waflib.Node
@@ -338,7 +338,7 @@ def load_module(path,encoding=None):
 		return cache_modules[path]
 	except KeyError:
 		pass
-	module=imp.new_module(WSCRIPT_FILE)
+	module=types.ModuleType(WSCRIPT_FILE)
 	try:
 		code=Utils.readf(path,encoding=encoding)
 	except EnvironmentError:
--
2.34.1
